        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0366" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1503.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Commissioner Fort to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santo Domingo</hi>
                        </placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1914-09-03T16:00:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1914-08-31T00:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date><hi rendition="#italic">; received September 3,
                            1914, 4 p.m.]</hi>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Yesterday we took up the Arias situation with Provisional President. He asked
                    that he be granted a few days to handle it himself. Today he advised he had word
                    from Arias agreeing to acknowledge his authority and to disband at once.
                    Everything is getting so much better here advise letting Provisional President
                    handle it at present. Commission is in daily touch with situation. We get many
                    inaccurate reports from those who send them from various motives. Arias can be
                    gotten much more surely and easily after Báez arranges than now. Advise awaiting
                    action by Báez, we keeping in touch with situation. President Báez swore in his
                    Cabinet today and presented them to us.</p>
                <p>Tomorrow we get committee of Cabinet to discuss election plans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
